## Installation

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="bash"}
---
code: |
  pnpm add @talex-touch/tuffex
---
:::

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="typescript"}
---
code: |
  import { TxFlowchart } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/flowchart'
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/flowchart/style.css'
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/base.css'
---
:::

## Usage

### Basic workflow

Provide custom card markup through the `#node` slot; dragging a card snaps its landing position to the dot grid while connectors, anchor ports and signal beams follow measured card geometry.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartFlowchartDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Order workflow" description="A trigger and condition branch whose connector recomputes from measured card heights as you drag."}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const nodes = ref([
    { id: 'trigger', label: 'Trigger', tone: 'violet', x: 240, y: 20 },
    { id: 'branch', label: 'If / Else', tone: 'orange', x: 240, y: 178 },
  ])

  const edges = [
    { from: 'trigger', to: 'branch', tone: 'violet', pulse: true, label: 'payload', markerEnd: 'arrow' },
  ]

  function place({ id, x, y }) {
    const node = nodes.value.find(n => n.id === id)
    if (node) {
      node.x = x
      node.y = y
    }
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxFlowchart :nodes="nodes" :edges="edges" draggable ports @node-move="place">
      <template #node="{ node }">
        <!-- Custom card content; omit slot to use built-in title / description fields -->
      </template>
    </TxFlowchart>
  </template>
---
:::

### Edge curves, markers, canvas patterns and effects

Switch `edgeType` (`bezier` / `smoothstep` / `straight`), `edgeMarker` (`arrow` / `dot` / `none`), `background` (`dots` / `lines` / `cross` / `none`), and live `pulse` beams, `animated` marching dashes, and `ports` in real time.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartEdgesDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Edge routing & effects lab" description="Combine semantic connector tones, midpoint pill labels, directional markers and pulse beams; click any edge to fire edge-click."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxFlowchart
      :nodes="nodes"
      :edges="[
        { from: 'gateway', to: 'cache', tone: 'green', pulse: true, animated: true, label: 'HIT · 4ms' },
        { from: 'gateway', to: 'origin', tone: 'accent', pulse: true, label: 'MISS · 42ms' },
        { from: 'origin', to: 'fallback', tone: 'orange', dashed: true, label: 'Timeout fallback' },
      ]"
      edge-type="bezier"
      edge-marker="arrow"
      background="dots"
      ports
      draggable
      @edge-click="onEdgeClick"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Horizontal pipeline & live run states

Set `direction="horizontal"` to anchor connectors on the left and right edges of cards; pair node `status` (`running` / `success` / `warning` / `error`) with pulsing edges to drive live CI/CD execution timelines.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartPipelineDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Horizontal CI/CD release pipeline" description="Run the pipeline or simulate a test failure to observe running halos, signal pulses and blocked downstream edges."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxFlowchart
      ref="flowRef"
      :nodes="stages"
      :edges="links"
      direction="horizontal"
      edge-marker="arrow"
      :selected-id="selectedId"
      ports
      pannable
      zoomable
      controls
      @node-click="({ id }) => (selectedId = id)"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### AI Agent multi-branch orchestration

Compose intent routing, vector retrieval, SQL tools, sandbox execution and streaming synthesis on one DAG; switch routing strategies to highlight active branches and inspect any node.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartAgentDemo" code-lang="vue" title="AI Agent orchestration canvas" description="Switch between single-tool routes or full parallel fan-out and click any node to inspect its role and metrics."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxFlowchart
      :nodes="agentNodes"
      :edges="agentEdges"
      edge-marker="arrow"
      :selected-id="selectedId"
      ports
      pannable
      zoomable
      controls
      @node-click="({ id }) => (selectedId = id)"
      @canvas-click="selectedId = null"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Pan, zoom, minimap and snap guides

Enable `pannable`, `zoomable`, `controls` and `minimap` for full viewport navigation; dragging reveals alignment snap guides against peer nodes and `fitView()` frames dynamic additions automatically.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartCanvasDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Interactive viewport & minimap playground" description="Drag empty space to pan, Ctrl/⌘ + wheel to zoom, click the minimap to jump, and append nodes with automatic framing."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxFlowchart
      ref="flowRef"
      :nodes="nodes"
      :edges="edges"
      background="cross"
      edge-marker="arrow"
      draggable
      ports
      pannable
      zoomable
      controls
      minimap
      @node-move="place"
      @viewport-change="onViewportChange"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Orthogonal approval & fallback state machine

Combine `edgeType="smoothstep"` with `background="lines"` for structured risk gates, human sign-off loops and rollback paths.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="FlowchartApprovalDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Risk-gated release approval flow" description="Switch between low, medium and high risk scores to illuminate the active smoothstep path and node status."}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxFlowchart
      :nodes="approvalNodes"
      :edges="approvalEdges"
      edge-type="smoothstep"
      background="lines"
      edge-marker="arrow"
      ports
      pannable
      zoomable
      controls
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Best Practices

- Align vertical backbone nodes on the same `x` and horizontal lanes on the same `y` so primary connectors read as clean straight runs.
- Let card content drive its own height; avoid pinning `height` on cards so `ResizeObserver` keeps ports and edges accurate.
- Pass `title`, `description`, `meta` and `badge` for concise declarative cards, and reserve the `#node` slot for bespoke token builders or forms.
- Use `node.tone` on chips to name the **kind of step** and `node.status` to signal **execution state** (`running`, `success`, `warning`, `error`).
- Call `flowRef.value?.fitView()` after mounting wide horizontal pipelines or mutating nodes so narrow viewports never clip cards.

## API Reference

### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `nodes` | `FlowNode[]` | — | Nodes placed on the canvas. Required. |
| `edges` | `FlowEdge[]` | `[]` | Directed connectors between nodes. |
| `height` | `number` | `333` | Canvas height in px. |
| `nodeWidth` | `number` | `290` | Default node width, overridable per `FlowNode.width`. |
| `grid` | `number` | `22` | Grid pitch and drag snap step in px. |
| `dots` | `boolean` | `true` | Render the dot grid when `background` is unset. |
| `background` | `FlowBackground` | — | Canvas backdrop pattern: `dots` / `lines` / `cross` / `none`. |
| `direction` | `FlowDirection` | `'vertical'` | Connector anchor axis: `vertical` (top/bottom) or `horizontal` (left/right). |
| `edgeType` | `FlowEdgeType` | `'bezier'` | Default connector curve: `bezier` / `smoothstep` / `straight`. |
| `edgeMarker` | `FlowEdgeMarker` | `'none'` | Default endpoint marker: `none` / `arrow` / `dot`. |
| `ports` | `boolean` | `false` | Render anchor port dots on connected card edges. |
| `selectedId` | `string \| null` | `null` | Controlled selected node id. |
| `draggable` | `boolean` | `false` | Allow dragging nodes. |
| `snap` | `boolean` | `true` | Snap dragged nodes to the grid pitch. |
| `snapGuides` | `boolean` | `true` | Show alignment hairlines while dragging in line with peer nodes. |
| `pannable` | `boolean` | `false` | Allow dragging empty canvas space to pan the viewport. |
| `zoomable` | `boolean` | `false` | Allow `Ctrl/⌘ + wheel` and HUD zoom. |
| `minZoom` | `number` | `0.45` | Minimum zoom scale. |
| `maxZoom` | `number` | `1.75` | Maximum zoom scale. |
| `controls` | `boolean` | `false` | Render the bottom-right zoom & fit-view HUD. |
| `minimap` | `boolean` | `false` | Render a live clickable SVG minimap in the bottom-left corner. |
| `ariaLabel` | `string` | `'Workflow'` | Accessible name for the canvas region. |
| `labels` | `FlowchartLabels` | `{}` | Localized accessible labels for HUD buttons and minimap. |

### Types

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="typescript"}
---
code: |
  type FlowNodeTone = 'violet' | 'orange' | 'accent' | 'green' | 'red' | 'neutral'
  type FlowNodeStatus = 'idle' | 'active' | 'running' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'error'
  type FlowEdgeType = 'bezier' | 'smoothstep' | 'straight'
  type FlowEdgeMarker = 'none' | 'arrow' | 'dot'
  type FlowDirection = 'vertical' | 'horizontal'
  type FlowBackground = 'dots' | 'lines' | 'cross' | 'none'

  interface FlowNode {
    id: string
    x: number
    y: number
    label?: string
    tone?: FlowNodeTone
    width?: number
    draggable?: boolean
    status?: FlowNodeStatus
    selected?: boolean
    ports?: boolean
    title?: string
    description?: string
    meta?: string
    badge?: string
  }

  interface FlowEdge {
    id?: string
    from: string
    to: string
    type?: FlowEdgeType
    tone?: FlowNodeTone
    dashed?: boolean
    animated?: boolean
    pulse?: boolean
    active?: boolean
    label?: string
    markerEnd?: FlowEdgeMarker
  }
---
:::

### Events

| Name | Payload | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `node-move` | `{ id, x, y }` | A node finished dragging. The host must write coordinates back to persist the move. |
| `node-click` | `{ id, node }` | A node was clicked or activated via Enter / Space (suppressed after a >4px drag). |
| `edge-click` | `{ edge, index }` | A connector or its midpoint label pill was clicked. |
| `canvas-click` | — | Empty canvas background was clicked, useful for clearing selection. |
| `viewport-change` | `{ x, y, zoom }` | Emitted whenever panning, zooming, `fitView` or `resetView` updates the camera. |

### Slots

| Name | Scope | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `node` | `{ node, index }` | Custom card body. Falls back to built-in structured layout when `title`/`description`/`meta`/`badge` are supplied. |
| `label` | `{ node }` | Replaces the category chip above a node. |
| `edge-label` | `{ edge, index }` | Custom content inside an edge's midpoint pill. |
| `toolbar` | `{ zoom, zoomIn, zoomOut, fitView, resetView }` | Replaces the default bottom-right HUD toolbar. |
| `empty` | — | Empty state rendered when `nodes` is empty. |

### Exposed Methods

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `fitView` | `(padding?: number) => void` | Frame and centre all nodes inside the current canvas bounds. |
| `zoomIn` | `() => void` | Step zoom in by +15% around the canvas centre. |
| `zoomOut` | `() => void` | Step zoom out by −15% around the canvas centre. |
| `resetView` | `() => void` | Reset viewport pan to `(0, 0)` and zoom to `100%`. |
| `centerOn` | `(nodeId: string) => void` | Centre the viewport on a specific node id. |
| `getViewport` | `() => FlowViewport` | Return the current `{ x, y, zoom }` viewport transform. |

## Coordinates

`x` is the node's **horizontal centre** and `y` is its **top edge** in canvas CSS pixels. In vertical mode connectors run from the bottom centre of `from` to the top edge of `to`'s card; in horizontal mode they run from the right midpoint of `from`'s card to the left midpoint of `to`'s card, all driven by `ResizeObserver`.

`grid` controls both the backdrop pattern pitch and the drag snap increment, scaling and shifting smoothly with the viewport camera.

## Connectors

Edges support `bezier`, `smoothstep` (with rounded corners and clean backward detours), and `straight` geometry. `pulse` renders a dual-layer luminous beam using SVG `pathLength="100"` so travel speed stays uniform across any curve shape and never clips on axis-aligned straight lines.

Edges referencing an unknown node id are skipped automatically.

## Overview

- **Always controlled:** the component never mutates `nodes` or `edges`. Drag deltas are held transiently and reported on release via `node-move`, with a 4px movement threshold suppressing spurious `node-click` events.
- **Scroll-safe zooming:** `zoomable` listens only to `Ctrl / ⌘ + wheel` and HUD buttons so ordinary page scrolling is never trapped.
- **Reduced motion compliant:** marching dashes, signal pulse beams and running-node halos are gated under `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`, preserving clear static cues when motion is reduced.
- **Accessible interaction:** every node is keyboard-focusable (`Enter` / `Space` → `node-click`, `aria-selected`), the SVG connector layer carries `aria-hidden="true"`, and edge labels plus HUD controls use native `<button type="button">`.

